:- module(tc, [go/0]).
:- chr_constraint go/0.
:- function mystery/1.
mystery(X) -> X.
% X is a local variable — a fresh flexible — and mystery/1's return
% type is `any`, which binds nothing: X stays flexible after the
% `is`. The following unifications then bind X to int and fail
% against the string. (Under the pre-spec behavior, the `is` stamped
% X to `any` and both unifications passed silently.)
bad @ go <=> X is mystery(1), X = 1, X = "s".
